  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656588",
      "title": "Understanding the \"async\" Pipe",
      "lectureOrder": 574,
      "videoOrder": 527,
      "sourceHash": "c9939781a8b63ce5ff3b34cd72047361ad31c2b155f6d4a8ab1e6dac762c139a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.43,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "-: In this module, we learned a lot about pipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "what they are, how to use them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 7.44,
          "en": "how to parameterize them, how to chain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.44,
          "end": 9.93,
          "en": "and how to create our own pipes, and how to maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.93,
          "end": 14.46,
          "en": "create an impure pipe forcing update on each data change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.46,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "Now there's one built-in pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "I want to have a closer look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 20.91,
          "en": "which does something different than all the other pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.91,
          "end": 23.61,
          "en": "It helps us with handling asynchronous data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.61,
          "end": 25.71,
          "en": "And to demonstrate how this works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.71,
          "end": 30.44,
          "en": "let's say we have another property right here at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.44,
          "end": 35.44,
          "en": "which says app status, or which holds our app status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 38.31,
          "en": "which could also be offline, critical, or whatever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.31,
          "end": 42.06,
          "en": "but here, this will not be a string like offline.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 44.22,
          "en": "Instead, this should get loaded after,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.22,
          "end": 45.6,
          "en": "let's say, two seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.6,
          "end": 48.48,
          "en": "And to simulate this, I will set this equal to a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.48,
          "end": 50.85,
          "en": "And you can imagine this data being returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.85,
          "end": 52.8,
          "en": "from a http call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.8,
          "end": 55.11,
          "en": "from a server, something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.11,
          "end": 57.96,
          "en": "So in this promise, I will initialize this promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.96,
          "end": 62.25,
          "en": "with a call back method passed to the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.25,
          "end": 64.89,
          "en": "where this method itself takes two arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.89,
          "end": 66.72,
          "en": "resolve and reject, the two functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.72,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "we can execute inside of this promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "to resolve or reject the promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 74.19,
          "en": "And in the promise in this callback function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.19,
          "end": 76.23,
          "en": "I will then set up a timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.23,
          "end": 78.57,
          "en": "Let's say it triggers after two seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.57,
          "end": 80.78999999999999,
          "en": "So after 2000 milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.78999999999999,
          "end": 83.55,
          "en": "And then this method here will get executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 83.55,
          "end": 86.76,
          "en": "This method, I passed to the set time out method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 86.76,
          "end": 88.366,
          "en": "Now here in this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 88.366,
          "end": 92.94,
          "en": "I want to simply set my app status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 96.3,
          "en": "So I want to resolve to, let's say, stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 98.37,
          "en": "whatever the status should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.37,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "So what this will do is it will set app status to stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 104.49000000000001,
          "en": "but only after two seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.49000000000001,
          "end": 107.72999999999999,
          "en": "So if we try to output this app status here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.72999999999999,
          "end": 109.25999999999999,
          "en": "let's add a line break,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.25999999999999,
          "end": 112.59,
          "en": "or another line break to have a blank line in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.59,
          "end": 115.83,
          "en": "and then a heading where I say app status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.83,
          "end": 118.08,
          "en": "And then I try to output app status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.08,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "with string interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 122.67,
          "en": "If we do this, you see object Object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 124.92,
          "en": "And this is correct because it is our object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.92,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "It's a promise, and a promise is our object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 130.23,
          "en": "But after two seconds, we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "that this is no longer an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "It now is a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 138.06,
          "en": "but angler doesn't know because it doesn't watch our object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 141.63,
          "en": "It doesn't see if this object actually transforms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.63,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "to something else, or if this returns as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "It just knows, it's a promise, I'm done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "And it's good that it behaves like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 151.07999999999998,
          "en": "Saves us performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 153.63,
          "en": "We should be explicit about how our app behaves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 153.63,
          "end": 158.63,
          "en": "But thankfully there is a nice little pipe we can use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 158.67000000000002,
          "end": 163.47,
          "en": "to make the transformation of this data easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "We know that it will be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 168.32999999999998,
          "en": "after two seconds and we want to output this string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.32999999999998,
          "end": 171.6,
          "en": "or it will resolve a string after two seconds, I should say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 173.52,
          "en": "and we want to output this string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.52,
          "end": 175.71,
          "en": "so we can add the pipe symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 175.71,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "and then async.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 179.55,
          "en": "This is a built-in pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 179.55,
          "end": 182.943,
          "en": "and by adding it, well, watch for yourself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.81,
          "end": 186.78,
          "en": "You see, I will reload the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 189.06,
          "en": "There's nothing there at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 189.06,
          "end": 191.88,
          "en": "but after two seconds you see stable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 194.19,
          "en": "And this is what async does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.19,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "It recognizes that this is a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "And as a side note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "it put all the work with observables there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 205.165,
          "en": "It would subscribe automatically, and after two seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 205.165,
          "end": 209.67000000000002,
          "en": "it will simply recognize that something changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 210.99,
          "en": "that the promise resolved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 210.99,
          "end": 212.79,
          "en": "Or in the case of an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 212.79,
          "end": 215.61,
          "en": "that data was sent through the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 215.61,
          "end": 219.03,
          "en": "and it will print this data to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 219.03,
          "end": 220.98,
          "en": "And this is the pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 220.98,
          "end": 224.31,
          "en": "with which I want to conclude this section about pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 224.31,
          "end": 227.43,
          "en": "Now you should feel really comfortable about using them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 227.43,
          "end": 230.67000000000002,
          "en": "building your own pipes, and, as you see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 230.67000000000002,
          "end": 233.28,
          "en": "working with async data with pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 233.28,
          "end": 235.41,
          "en": "Now we will see this async pipe being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 235.41,
          "end": 238.44,
          "en": "in the http section later, but for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 238.44,
          "end": 241.743,
          "en": "let's move on to some exercises regarding pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
